 subset of it (all IDs overlap) for runs in the rendered UI, which the code README describes as a local multi-app web environment driven through Playwright; seeds holds 36 disjoint hand-written scenarios. The card says source is seed or mcts, but every released row reads seed or legacy_pilot_seed. The code repository linked as ukplab/arxiv2026-agentcibench now resolves to UKPLab/emnlp2026-agentcibench (GitHub API), and the card's second code link, agentcibench/agentcibench, returns 404. The 67.9% average leakage over 15 agents is a publisher figure. CC BY 4.0 is the card's data declaration; the code is a separate Apache-2.0 release.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/UKPLab/agentcibench/raw/f5523cb986828ee77bc505120a933f114bbcf4f3/README.md","target_id":"arxiv:2606.23189","type":"documented_by"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Contextual-integrity benchmark for computer-use agents: 117 synthetic multi-app workspace scenarios that pair under-specified requests with must-share and must-not-share lists, plus a 50-scenario live-UI subset.","task_classes":["R01.05.02.01"],"topics":["evaluation","safety-security","cross-app"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/UKPLab/agentcibench"}
